Tier 5 -- adapter conformance, shape B (reaper guest, real CBSD).

One conformance suite run against both the mock adapter and the real one,
asserting identical contracts: same fields, same error shapes, same exit-code
discipline. The real side drives an actual jail through its lifecycle. This is
the tier that breaks first when CBSD changes an invocation convention.
See TESTING.md §6.

Empty at M0. The guest prologue (tests/lib/guest-prologue.sh) that installs and
pins CBSD already runs, so the substrate this tier needs is proven before the
tier exists.

Files named t_*.sh are tests; anything else here is ignored.
